From c2fe431a1a4a313eed28e87a2fdfabeb8b5a839a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:01:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Audit 2026-09-04: refuse non-English RFQs, keep clarification
 context, unblock the event loop, harden price entry, fix prose/SFP28 parsing

- new_path/service.py: NON_ENGLISH_INPUT guard (Cyrillic text used to yield a
  silently reduced, approvable plan); looks_like_full_rfq needs two independent
  signals so short clarification answers no longer restart the request; public
  entry points serialised with an RLock; price range error says EUR.
- bot/handlers.py: planner calls run via asyncio.to_thread; price parsing
  handles thousands/decimal separators and accepts only price-shaped messages;
  a new RFQ typed while a price is pending starts a fresh request; /prices
  prompts say EUR (pricing has been EUR end to end since fe179f6); stale
  /start and /quote copy.
- parsing/normalize.py: number words and "dual" before components or numbers,
  "N processors", "dual-socket", terabyte memory and "GB of memory".
- parsing/extractors/network.py: sfp28 before sfp\\+? so 25GbE SFP28 is not
  normalised to SFP+; one requirement per (ports, speed) instead of duplicates.
- parsing/extractors/storage.py: usable pools take media/protocol from the
  rest of the clause; the drive-pack guard window stops at the clause boundary.
- main.py: clear startup error when the configurator workbook is missing.
- Dockerfile/docker-compose: drop the non-existent templates directory.
- docs/AUDIT_2026-09-04.md: findings, fixes, open items, verification on the
  real workbook; CLAUDE.md pointer.
- tests/test_audit_2026_09_regressions.py: 58 workbook-free regressions.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
